        <briefdescription>
<para>Loads or retrieves a shader program by name. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If the shader has already been compiled and cached under the given name, returns the cached instance. Otherwise, compiles the shader from source strings and stores it in the cache.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>name</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unique identifier for this shader (e.g., &quot;sprite&quot;, &quot;ui&quot;). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>vertexSource</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>GLSL source code for the vertex shader. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fragmentSource</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>GLSL source code for the fragment shader. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Shared pointer to the loaded <ref refid="classShader" kindref="compound">Shader</ref>, or nullptr on compilation failure.</para>
</simplesect>
This method caches shaders by name, allowing the same shader to be used by multiple entities without recompiling. This is particularly useful for shaders that are used frequently (e.g., the standard sprite shader).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>name</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Unique identifier for this shader. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>vertexSource</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>GLSL source code for the vertex shader. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fragmentSource</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>GLSL source code for the fragment shader. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Shared pointer to the loaded <ref refid="classShader" kindref="compound">Shader</ref>, or nullptr on compilation failure. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
